  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1205 AM CDT Sat Jul 18 2026\n\nA weak remnant disturbance aloft will be over far West Texas on \nSunday. With weak lift and some remaining moisture east of this low, \na few showers and thunderstorms will be possible Sunday afternoon in \nthe our western counties, mainly west of a Rotan to Robert Lee to \nOzona line. Highs on Sunday are expected to be mostly in the lower \n90s, with a few upper 80s in the Northern Edwards Plateau.  \n\nOur area will see a pattern more typical of mid-summer next week, \nwith hotter and drier conditions. A fairly large upper level high \nwill be shifting out of the central Rockies and over the southern \nPlains and North Texas. The high is forecast to be centered over the \nRed River Wednesday into Friday. Highs Monday will range from around \n90 in the Northern Edwards Plateau, to the mid 90s in most of the \nConcho Valley and Big Country. With an increasing trend in \ntemperatures through the week, highs Thursday and Friday are \nexpected to range from the lower/mid 90s in our southern counties, \nto 100-103 degrees in much of the Big Country and portions of the \nnorthwestern Concho Valley.",
